{"title":"How plants make food using sunlight","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make their own food in their leaves, and release oxygen as a by-product.","method":["Leaves contain a green pigment called chlorophyll that traps sunlight energy.","Plant roots absorb water from the soil.","Leaves take in carbon dioxide gas from the air through tiny holes called stomata.","Chlorophyll uses the sunlight energy to combine water and carbon dioxide into food (glucose) for the plant.","Oxygen is released back into the air as a waste product that animals and humans breathe."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant sits in sunlight by a window. Explain what it needs to make food and what it releases.","steps":["The plant's leaves contain chlorophyll to capture the sunlight coming through the window.","Water travels up from the roots in the soil to the leaves.","Carbon dioxide enters the leaves from the air around the plant.","Chlorophyll uses sunlight energy to turn water and carbon dioxide into food.","Oxygen is released into the room as the plant makes its food."],"answer":"The plant uses sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide to make food in its leaves, and releases oxygen."},"key_terms":[{"term":"Photosynthesis","meaning":"The process by which plants make their own food using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide."},{"term":"Chlorophyll","meaning":"The green pigment in leaves that captures sunlight energy."},{"term":"Stomata","meaning":"Tiny holes in leaves through which plants take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen."}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants get all their food from soil instead of making it themselves using sunlight.","Forgetting that plants need sunlight—they cannot make food in complete darkness."],"remember":"Sunlight + water + carbon dioxide = food (glucose) + oxygen.","quick_check":[{"q":"Where in the plant does photosynthesis happen?","a":"In the leaves, where chlorophyll is found."},{"q":"Name two things a plant takes in to make food.","a":"Water and carbon dioxide (or any two of: sunlight, water, carbon dioxide)."}],"tell_your_child":"Think of leaves as tiny food factories—they use sunshine, water, and air to cook up food for the whole plant. The best part is, while the plant eats, it also gives us oxygen to breathe!","picture":{"concept_key":"c5-biology-photosynthesis","scene_prompt":"A bright sunny day with a leafy green plant near a window, water droplets on soil below, and a child breathing fresh air nearby."}}
```
